ilya2@rcn.com wrote:
> Thanks! One more question -- what about AC bonuses I get from donating
> to priests? If I donate while a vampire, will the bonus remain or not?
AC bonuses from donation will remain. By the same token, any actions
that causes you to lose your protection will also stick. The same is
true of alignment, luck, prayer timeout, etc.

There are times when being polymorphed has potential indirect
consequences on alignment and/or prayer. As a chaotic monk, I can't
think of a case where being an undead can get you in trouble with your
god. Being a demon is okay too, unless you genocide something as a
chaotic demon (-1 to alignment). Even that is minor issue, though.
Lawfuls and neutrals should avoid praying as a demon or undead. It
never succeeds for lawfuls, and only rarely succeeds for neutrals. They
should also avoid accidentally sacrificing their own base race while
polymorphed, but that's another thing you don't have to worry about as
a chaotic. You should probably avoid polymorphing into a purple worm,
though - digesting non veggy creatures breaks vegetarian/vegan conduct.



